    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-70313",
      "knowledge_point_id": "e5c108c0-f32a-5725-af3b-c3e747da09f2",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating Binomial Coefficients Using the Formula",
      "problem": "Determine the value of $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{4}).$",
      "worked_solution": "The binomial coefficient $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{r})$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{r})=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $n=7$ and $r=4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{4}) & =\\frac{7!}{(7-4)!\\cdot 4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5\\cdot 4!}{3!\\cdot 4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot \\cancel{6}\\cdot 5\\cdot \\cancel{4!}}{\\cancel{6}\\cdot \\cancel{4!}} \\\\  & =7\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =35.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
