    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-113616",
      "knowledge_point_id": "e5c108c0-f32a-5725-af3b-c3e747da09f2",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating Binomial Coefficients Using the Formula",
      "problem": "Determine the value of $(\\frac{9}{6}).$",
      "worked_solution": "The binomial coefficient $(\\frac{n}{r})$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n(\\frac{n}{r})=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $n=9$ and $r=6.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{9}{6}) & =\\frac{9!}{(9-6)!\\cdot 6!} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\cdot 8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6!}{3!\\cdot 6!} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\cdot 8\\cdot 7\\cdot \\cancel{6!}}{6\\cdot \\cancel{6!}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\cdot 8\\cdot 7}{6} \\\\  & =84.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
